@project:P{br=~199:Evaluate whether candidate.png is ready to become the baseline sprite for the rest of the robot family. The agreed visual identity is reference.png. Inputs are 32x32 RGBA sprites in the project root.;in=[@i-canvas,@i-palette,@i-alpha,@i-view,@i-identity,@i-identity-features,@i-destination];nm=~28:Robot family baseline review;ow=@user;sc=[@s-assignment,@s-reference]}
@q-baseline-fitness:Q{ck=~226:The sprite is a sound starting point to derive sibling robots from: its identity features are the reference's, and any asymmetry present is a deliberate design feature rather than a dropped element that siblings would inherit.;dm=other;md=visual;nm=~30:Fitness as the family baseline;so=[@s-assignment];wh=@actor}
@q-identity:Q{ck=~321:Inspected enlarged beside reference.png, the candidate carries the agreed identity: both head antennae present, both eyes present, and the silhouette bilaterally symmetric about the sprite centre as in the reference. A feature the reference has and the candidate drops is a failure even when colours and dimensions match.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~34:Identity fidelity to reference.png;so=[@s-reference,@s-assignment];wh=@actor}
@q-mechanical:Q{ck=~140:32x32 RGBA; every visible pixel is one of #25354A, #56B5BC or #F4DDA2; zero fractional-alpha pixels; exactly one connected opaque component.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~31:Mechanical contract conformance;so=[@s-assignment];wh=@actor}
@s-assignment:S{at=~25:2026-09-11T00:00:00+00:00;au=local;dg=~64:8669aaabd4383d1634c764457ddf3a7bf61d3de757020ca502f36c7fa19916fc;ln=[];ur=~32:pixl-state/sources/assignment.md}
@s-reference:S{at=~25:2026-09-11T00:00:00+00:00;au=local;dg=~64:d997cadefc6b94c1c14f4ec17159deaf5ceb7ea9543b2522390ea1a577470aa7;ln=[];ur=~13:reference.png}
@t-sample:T{ca=[@x-candidate-1];dc=[];dp=[];ip=[@x-reference];kn=[];nm=~55:Review candidate.png for the robot family baseline role;op=[@f-baseline];ow=@actor;ph=sample;pr=@project;st=active;vr=[@v-mech-1,@v-identity-1,@v-fitness-1]}
@user:A{nm=~13:Project owner;rl=user}
@v-fitness-1:V{at=~25:2026-09-11T00:00:00+00:00;ev=[@e-visual-1];rq=@q-baseline-fitness;st=fail;tk=@t-sample;wh=@actor;wy=~419:Not fit as the family baseline. The two missing features are dropped elements rather than a deliberate design, and a baseline propagates: every sibling robot derived from it would inherit the missing antenna and missing eye, and the error would then look like the family's intended identity rather than a defect. Mechanical conformance is exactly why this needed a visual check: dimensions and palette cannot detect it.;xr=@x-candidate-1}
@v-identity-1:V{at=~25:2026-09-11T00:00:00+00:00;ev=[@e-visual-1];rq=@q-identity;st=fail;tk=@t-sample;wh=@actor;wy=~754:Rejected on identity. Enlarged 12x three-panel comparison (reference | candidate | per-pixel difference) was inspected directly. The candidate drops two identity features that reference.png has:
1. The left head antenna is gone: 24 outline pixels at x7-10, y3-8 are #25354A in the reference and fully transparent in the candidate. The candidate reads as a one-antenna robot.
2. The right eye is gone: 12 accent pixels at x18-20, y14-17 are #F4DDA2 in the reference and repainted body teal #56B5BC in the candidate. The candidate reads as one-eyed.
Only 36 of 1024 pixels differ and no pixel was added, so every mechanical measurement still passes. Mirror-test about the sprite centre: the reference's head and face are symmetric, the candidate's are not.;xr=@x-candidate-1}
@v-mech-1:V{at=~25:2026-09-11T00:00:00+00:00;ev=[@e-mech-1];rq=@q-mechanical;st=pass;tk=@t-sample;wh=@actor;wy=~347:Canvas, palette, binary alpha and single-component silhouette all conform. pixl_asset_check plus a local Pillow measurement of candidate.png: 32x32, 366 visible pixels in exactly the three confirmed palette colours (#56B5BC 198, #25354A 156, #F4DDA2 12), zero fractional-alpha pixels, one connected opaque component, no colour outside the palette.;xr=@x-candidate-1}
@x-candidate-1:X{ct=@contract;dg=~64:d28f90f619400f8a770741b23bb5c1da995e6b6dd017ebab30eac934892c8d8d;kd=sprite;nm=~51:Generated robot sample nominated as family baseline;of=@f-baseline;ur=~13:candidate.png}
